      "id": 1,
      "text": "German immigrant John Meiners, who ran a successful Milwaukee brewery, bought the land that would become Meiners Oaks in the 1870s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meiners_Oaks%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The purchase was made as payment for a debt, a transaction that gave the community its distinctive name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meiners_Oaks%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nestled in the heart of the Ojai Valley, Meiners Oaks lies just 70 miles north of Los Angeles and offers trails along the Ventura River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
